desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Rails Skip Forgery Protection"
	title_zh: "Rails Skip Forgery Protection"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-rails-skip-forgery-protection"
	risk: "csrf"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `rails-skip-forgery-protection` (ruby/rails/security/audit/rails-skip-forgery-protection.yaml).
Original message: This call turns off CSRF protection allowing CSRF attacks against the application
CWE: CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)
References:
- https://api.rubyonrails.org/classes/ActionController/RequestForgeryProtection/ClassMethods.html#method-i-skip_forgery_protection
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.rb": <<<POS
skip_forgery_protection
POS
	"safefile://pos.rb": <<<NEG
protect_forgery_protection
NEG
)

${*.rb}.pattern_regex(/(?:skip_forgery_protection)/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Rails Skip Forgery Protection",
	title_zh: "Rails Skip Forgery Protection",
	message: "Rails Skip Forgery Protection detected.",
}
